[261.416,"o","$ "]
[261.416,"o","ov stack deploy openvidu-e2e-oci-ha-s124040 --cloud oracle --mode auto\r\n"]
[262.436,"o","warning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one\r\n"]
[262.439,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[262.443,"o","   · read Terraform's plan of applying .openvidu/oracle again (nothing is changed)\r\n"]
[268.519,"o","This is what ov does in your Oracle Cloud tenancy (region eu-madrid-1, compartment ***); --debug shows every command:\r\n\r\n  1. Template: render the high availability template into .openvidu/oracle/tf-oracle-openvidu-pro-ha.tf\r\n     and its variables into .openvidu/oracle/openvidu.auto.tfvars.json (0600)\r\n  2. Machines: they already exist; Terraform's plan changes nothing, so applying again only refreshes what the stack outputs\r\n  3. Wait for OpenVidu to be up, read what it published (URL, credentials) and register this directory as the stack\r\n\r\nWarning: the stack publishes into the vault *** (--oci-vault), which is not its own. Its secrets have fixed names (OPENVIDU_URL, the credentials, the license, the stack's access), so two stacks in one vault mix them; every deploy adds versions to the same secrets until Oracle refuses more (LimitExceeded) and the stack never publishes; and a destroy leaves this stack's credentials in it. Give every stack a vault of its own: leave --oci-vault out and the stack creates one.\r\n\r\n"]
[268.67,"o","Run these in your account? Only yes or y goes ahead [y/N]: "]
[268.67,"o","yes\r\n"]
[268.67,"o","\r\n▶ Create the machines on Oracle Cloud…\r\n   · initialize Terraform in .openvidu/oracle (downloads the provider)\r\n"]
[269.374,"o","   · apply .openvidu/oracle (this returns when Terraform is done)\r\n"]
[274.266,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so `ov stack destroy` removes it even if the wait below fails\r\n   ✓ Create the machines on Oracle Cloud\r\n\r\n▶ Wait for the machines to deploy OpenVidu…\r\n"]
